1
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:12,200
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:41,467
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:44,267
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:45,367
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,800
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,333
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,933
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:55,600
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:58,300
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,467
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:03,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:06,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:12,000
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,300
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:22,967
<i>I'm just hoping
you'll sign this document.</i>

21
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:24,967
<i> I won't sign that document.</i>

22
00:01:24,967 --> 00:01:26,667
<i>My father won't agree to that.
Get out!</i>

23
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:28,300
<i>This won't help you.
If you sign this,</i>

24
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,000
<i> you will lose your home.</i>

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,467
<i> What do you know</i>

26
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:32,667
<i>- about this document?!
- They will pay for this!</i>

27
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:34,500
<i> Boss Mariano called me.</i>

28
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,833
<i> He'll have you picked up.</i>

29
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:38,467
<i>I have a chance to show
the Zafras what I'm capable of.</i>

30
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:40,200
<i>Is that enough to pin
the blame on Gabo?</i>

31
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,500
<i>- What else can identify Gabo?
- Motorcycle?</i>

32
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:44,233
I want one exactly like Gabo's.

33
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:45,867
<i>Now I'm getting
to know you better.</i>

34
00:01:45,867 --> 00:01:48,400
<i>You're genuinely humane
and loving toward others.</i>

35
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,900
<i> You've earned my admiration.</i>

36
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,267
Well, Betchay?

37
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:56,000
What if I signed that document?!

38
00:01:56,667 --> 00:01:57,733
Huh?!

39
00:01:57,733 --> 00:02:01,300
How would I even face
our neighbors?!

40
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,433
You'll bring disaster
to all of us!

41
00:02:05,433 --> 00:02:08,733
Sorry, Dy. I didn't know!

42
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,667
I just wanted to help you.

43
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:15,000
I didn't know that woman
will deceive me.

44
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:16,600
So use your brain!

45
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:20,267
You're going to put all of us
in danger!

46
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:22,233
Did you even think about that?!

47
00:02:22,967 --> 00:02:24,067
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

48
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:29,900
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,733
[KIDS]
Whoever's different is it!

50
00:02:31,733 --> 00:02:35,600
- [KIDS SCREAMING]
- [LAUGHTER]

51
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,967
- Be careful! You might slip!
- [WOMAN] Be careful!

52
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:46,000
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

53
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:48,700
[KULOT]
Come on, let's take a bath!

54
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:53,067
[HOPIA] It's really fun here
in Gabo's community!

55
00:02:53,067 --> 00:02:55,933
- We're always full!
- [KULOT] That's not all.

56
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:59,733
We're always full,
and we're even safe!

57
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:03,000
[BOKBOK] Of course!
Because Gabo is here.

58
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,100
- [BILOG] He's my idol!
- Mine too!

59
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:08,900
- He's my idol too!
- Gabo is my idol! There he is!

60
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:10,433
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

61
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:12,667
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

62
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:16,633
- Did you eat a lot?
- Yes, Gabo!

63
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,767
[BOKBOK]
Thank you so much, Gabo.

64
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:20,800
You saved our lives.

65
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,500
[KULOT] Bokbok's right.
Thank you very, very much!

66
00:03:23,533 --> 00:03:27,633
[PALITS] Thank you, Gabo!
We ate a lot.

67
00:03:27,633 --> 00:03:31,000
[BILOG] Thank you, Gabo!
I'm so full now!

68
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,433
You're welcome.

69
00:03:33,433 --> 00:03:35,800
It's slippery, so be careful
when running around.

70
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,633
- You might slip.
- Yes!

71
00:03:38,633 --> 00:03:42,100
- Let's go to the cars!
- Oh, yeah!

72
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,800
Hey, be careful!
Mister Elton might get mad!

73
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:47,100
- [KULOT] He won't!
- [ELTON] Where are you going?

74
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:50,100
- You might get stuck!
- We'll just get inside.

75
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,767
You're so naughty!

76
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:53,833
You might get into an accident!
Get out of there!

77
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:56,967
- We'll just play!
- You're too stubborn.

78
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:57,967
Gabo?

79
00:03:58,667 --> 00:04:00,533
Thank you very much.

80
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:01,800
If you hadn't arrived,

81
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,700
something bad might've
happened to me and Babot.

82
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:09,467
Gabo. Who were those men?

83
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:14,033
[GABO] Uh, love...

84
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,333
I don't know them either.

85
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,800
We talked about it earlier.

86
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,467
Could it be that they're
the ones harvesting organs?

87
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:26,633
That's possible.

88
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,967
But I don't know those guys.

89
00:04:30,767 --> 00:04:32,733
This only means one thing.

90
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:35,633
Outsiders have entered
our community.

91
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,833
That's why we all need
to be careful.

92
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:39,733
Love.

93
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:42,833
It's too dangerous
for all of us.

94
00:04:42,833 --> 00:04:44,467
So, if you can...

95
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,667
...don't leave the house
too much.

96
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:52,700
I think you should stay
in Paradise for now,

97
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,133
so I'm sure you're safe.

98
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,700
He's right, Gloria.
You should stay with us for now.

99
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,067
You will be safer here.

100
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:02,533
Besides, the people here
aren't familiar with you yet.

101
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:09,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:12,067
Why'd you choose this disguise?
We could've been something else.

103
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:13,967
I'm not the one
who came up with this!

104
00:05:13,967 --> 00:05:15,633
- It's Tomas!
- And you listened?

105
00:05:15,633 --> 00:05:16,967
You know
he likes playing with us!

106
00:05:16,967 --> 00:05:19,567
We could've texted Gabo!
Why do we have to find him?

107
00:05:19,567 --> 00:05:21,900
- Pops said to find him.
- Where do we go?

108
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,600
You want to be
a junk collector, right?

109
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,700
Then collect junk,

110
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,067
and ask around
where we should go.

111
00:05:26,067 --> 00:05:29,633
- We should've eaten at Gabo's!
- No! No one gets to eat!

112
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:31,733
[LAWIN] Where does he live?

113
00:05:31,733 --> 00:05:33,767
Last time I was here, it's night
and I wore a helmet.

114
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,100
- I couldn't see properly.
- Well, it's morning now.

115
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:39,567
We can't let something bad
happen again to Gabo.

116
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:40,967
Go and ask them then.

117
00:05:41,767 --> 00:05:43,467
Who among us is lacking?

118
00:05:43,467 --> 00:05:45,467
- [TEKLA] You tell me.
- Definitely not me.

119
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:48,100
Excuse me, where's the alley
headed to Paradise?

120
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,633
[MUSIC TURNS QUIRKY]

121
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:50,833
Do you guys know those two?

122
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:52,267
Who? Those two women?

123
00:05:52,267 --> 00:05:53,567
- No.
- I don't. Ouch!

124
00:05:53,567 --> 00:05:54,900
Those dirty-looking guys.

125
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,100
They're not from here.

126
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:57,600
Hurry up. Someone might spot us.

127
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,100
- Come on, let's ask them.
- Psst! Hey! Hey!

128
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:01,600
- Come on.
- Darn it. See?

129
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,100
- Hurry up!
- Hey, hey, hey!

130
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,967
- Hey! Stop them!
- Stop, you two!

131
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:09,500
Hey! Why are you here?

132
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:11,000
- We're just scavenging!
- You can't run away!

133
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,100
Why are you here?
You're clearly outsiders.

134
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,167
Tell the truth!

135
00:06:14,167 --> 00:06:17,800
- Where are you from?
- [STAMMERING]

136
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,267
- Where?!
- D-D-Divisioria!

137
00:06:19,267 --> 00:06:21,100
Divisoria! Divisoria!

138
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,800
That's pretty far.
Why are you here?

139
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,867
- B-Because...
- We're scavenging.

140
00:06:25,867 --> 00:06:27,133
We're scavenging junk.

141
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:30,100
Junk? Ginintuang Lupa's junkyard
is by the entrance!

142
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:31,300
These two are lying!

143
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,767
You bastards!

144
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,967
This is the first time
we've seen you around here.

145
00:06:34,967 --> 00:06:35,967
Why are you really here?

146
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:36,967
[STAMMERING]

147
00:06:36,967 --> 00:06:38,133
We're scavenging junk!

148
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:40,267
Hey! You're looking for Gabo,
aren't you?

149
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:41,600
You're probably
one of his enemies!

150
00:06:41,633 --> 00:06:43,000
Let's beat them up!

151
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:48,033
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [LAWIN, UWAK GROANING]

152
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:50,567
Come on!
Let's bring them to Gabo!

153
00:06:50,567 --> 00:06:52,200
Liars! You guys are enemies!

154
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,533
Quit fighting!

155
00:06:53,533 --> 00:06:55,533
Just come, jerks!

156
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,167
[BINOY] The other one
even pretends to stammer!

157
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:01,333
Do you think Django will succeed

158
00:07:01,333 --> 00:07:03,667
with the mission
the Zafras asked him to do?

159
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,167
He should.

160
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:10,000
Not everyone's
given a second chance.

161
00:07:10,667 --> 00:07:11,800
Besides,

162
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:15,033
if that happens,
we'll have a lot of money.

163
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:16,833
Ah. [CLAPS]

164
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:18,200
Great then.

165
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Having money
would definitely feel nice.

166
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,233
Romy, look for a motorcycle
for Django.

167
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:28,700
One that looks exactly
like Gabo's.

168
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,033
A motorcycle
that looks exactly like Gabo's.

169
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,200
- Yeah.
- Consider it done.

170
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,767
Men, let's go!

171
00:07:34,767 --> 00:07:36,733
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:07:36,733 --> 00:07:38,900
We need to get the job done.

173
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,600
If we succeed,

174
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,200
the Zafras will pay us
a huge sum

175
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,933
and we'll be able
to get back at Gabo.

176
00:07:43,933 --> 00:07:45,667
[CAR HONKING]

177
00:07:45,667 --> 00:07:47,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

178
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:48,900
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

179
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:51,367
[DOGS BARKING IN DISTANCE]

180
00:07:51,367 --> 00:07:53,300
- Are you Django?
- That's me.

181
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:54,300
Blindfold them!

182
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:56,067
- We didn't agree on this!
- Hurry!

183
00:07:56,067 --> 00:07:58,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:07:58,733 --> 00:08:00,733
[CAR DOOR CLOSES,
TIRES SCREECHING]

185
00:08:00,733 --> 00:08:03,733
[KIDS EXCLAIMING]

186
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,067
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:07,067
These kids are so stubborn!

188
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:08,600
- Whoo!
- Pretend you're driving!

189
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,200
Hey! Stop fidgeting!

190
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,133
- Whoo!
- This is fun!

191
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:14,067
[CAR CREAKING]

192
00:08:14,067 --> 00:08:15,067
I said stop fidgeting!

193
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:17,067
- Whoo!
- [CAR SEAT CREAKING]

194
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:18,700
- I said stop--
- [CAR HOOD THUDS]

195
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,733
- [BADONG SCREAMING] Agh!
- Badong! Badong!

196
00:08:20,733 --> 00:08:22,233
- What's that?
- What's happening?

197
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:23,967
[BADONG] Agh! Help me, Elton!

198
00:08:23,967 --> 00:08:25,067
The kids!

199
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:26,067
Check on the kids!

200
00:08:26,933 --> 00:08:27,967
- [SCREEN DOOR OPENS]
- What happened?

201
00:08:27,967 --> 00:08:29,933
Agh! Help me, Elton!

202
00:08:29,933 --> 00:08:32,100
[BADONG GROANING]

203
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,100
[CAR HOOD THUDS]

204
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,733
Badong, you alright?

205
00:08:36,267 --> 00:08:38,100
I'm fine, Gabo.

206
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,967
Are you kids alright?

207
00:08:40,067 --> 00:08:42,200
- Are you hurt?
- [BADONG] The hood fell.

208
00:08:42,267 --> 00:08:44,333
I don't know.
Maybe it's the kids.

209
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:46,267
You guys are so stubborn!

210
00:08:46,267 --> 00:08:48,400
You kids weren't listening!

211
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:50,267
I told you to stop fidgeting
many times!

212
00:08:50,267 --> 00:08:52,933
Uncle Elton, maybe you shouldn't
yell at the kids.

213
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:54,333
They might get traumatized.

214
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:57,467
Traumatized?
I'm the one traumatized by you!

215
00:08:57,467 --> 00:08:59,033
Look at what happened to Badong!

216
00:08:59,033 --> 00:09:00,367
He might need to be
brought to the hospital again!

217
00:09:00,367 --> 00:09:01,767
- We're sorry.
- We're sorry.

218
00:09:01,767 --> 00:09:04,267
You don't have to scream at us.

219
00:09:04,267 --> 00:09:05,800
We don't mean it.

220
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,433
[ELTON] Now I'm the bad guy!

221
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:09,767
You kids are at fault
and now I'm the bad guy!

222
00:09:09,767 --> 00:09:10,867
Uncle Elton, that's enough.

223
00:09:10,867 --> 00:09:13,267
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:14,933
Uncle Elton isn't mad at you.

225
00:09:15,933 --> 00:09:18,433
He just doesn't want you to get
hurt or get into an accident.

226
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,033
Gabo,

227
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:23,167
Elton, I'm really sorry
for the trouble.

228
00:09:23,167 --> 00:09:25,300
What did you kids do?
You can play but don't bother

229
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,367
- the people around you!
- [KIDS SOBBING]

230
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:28,267
Come on! Let's go home!

231
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:31,500
Gabo, thank you so much
for feeding the kids.

232
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,200
We'll go home now.

233
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:36,067
- Thank you, Gabo.
- We'll go home now.

234
00:09:36,067 --> 00:09:37,133
- Thank you, Gabo.
- We'll go now.

235
00:09:37,133 --> 00:09:39,333
Thank you so much.
We'll go home now.

236
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:46,300
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:58,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:09:58,700 --> 00:09:59,833
Bring them over!

239
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,333
Come here.

240
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:08,400
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

241
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,033
Remove their blindfolds.

242
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:10:18,267 --> 00:10:19,733
[DJANGO] Where are we?

244
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:21,367
What do you want from us?

245
00:10:21,367 --> 00:10:22,800
Pat them down.

246
00:10:27,567 --> 00:10:28,700
Boss.

247
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,900
Weapons aren't allowed.

248
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,500
That's just a low-caliber one.

249
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,867
Are you really going
to confiscate it?

250
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,500
What are you going
to do with us?

251
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,900
You have too many questions.

252
00:10:42,867 --> 00:10:45,033
- Bring them in.
- [MAN] Yes, boss.

253
00:10:45,033 --> 00:10:46,767
Wait there.

254
00:10:46,767 --> 00:10:48,567
Move it! Come on!

255
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,767
[DISTANT GUNSHOTS]

256
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:58,067
- What was that?
- Keep moving!

257
00:10:58,067 --> 00:11:01,333
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

258
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,033
I'm not my brother!

259
00:11:06,033 --> 00:11:07,333
[GUN COCKS]

260
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:13,933
But that doesn't mean
I'm useless!

261
00:11:14,967 --> 00:11:16,967
I'll prove it to you, Papa!

262
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:20,467
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

263
00:11:20,467 --> 00:11:21,833
Aah!

264
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:25,400
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

265
00:11:27,667 --> 00:11:30,433
I had Django summoned.

266
00:11:30,433 --> 00:11:32,600
I'll tell Lucas
to check on them.

267
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,467
Lucas has to be careful.

268
00:11:34,467 --> 00:11:37,333
He's not used to
handling people like Django.

269
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:42,400
He and his group are
used to all kinds of fights.

270
00:11:42,433 --> 00:11:45,500
They'll eat Lucas alive.

271
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:46,600
[GLASS THUDS]

272
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,667
It could be
the other way around.

273
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:51,967
They're entering Lucas's world.

274
00:11:51,967 --> 00:11:56,533
A world with money,
power, and connections.

275
00:11:56,533 --> 00:12:01,633
Things people like Django
spend their whole lives chasing.

276
00:12:02,667 --> 00:12:03,667
[SCOFFS]

277
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:08,967
[PIA]  My plan is underway.

278
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:14,567
<i>Team Alpha will slowly
turn against each other.</i>

279
00:12:19,033 --> 00:12:23,033
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:24,833
"I'm still observing them"

281
00:12:25,733 --> 00:12:28,467
[SEBASTIAN] I'm on a winning
streak with the Jacintos.

282
00:12:28,467 --> 00:12:29,700
I feel it.

283
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:31,533
Nothing will go wrong.

284
00:12:32,133 --> 00:12:35,200
But I'm not doing this
for myself.

285
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:38,967
I'm doing this to make the
NCIA look good to the Jacintos.

286
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:40,933
If you say so.

287
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,533
[PIA] <i> Anything that would lead
</i>you astray in the investigation,

288
00:12:45,533 --> 00:12:47,667
<i> I'll gladly accept.</i>

289
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:49,900
[CASTOR] Ma'am Pia,

290
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:52,033
it's possible that
the spy isn't from Team Alpha.

291
00:12:54,167 --> 00:12:56,500
But we still need to be careful.

292
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,633
Yes, ma'am.

293
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:02,867
What were you two
talking about, ma'am?

294
00:13:02,867 --> 00:13:05,000
I'm keeping tabs on Castor.

295
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,100
Do you think it's him?

296
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,067
Shh!

297
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:08,500
Keep it down.

298
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,733
[SIGHS]

299
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:12,000
Who do you think it is?

300
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,833
Give me some time.

301
00:13:13,833 --> 00:13:15,967
I'll find out who the mole is.

302
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,733
[EXHALES SHARPLY] Okay.

303
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,967
[SEQIOA]
Let me tell you this, Pia.

304
00:13:22,967 --> 00:13:26,700
They can hide,
but I'll find out who they are.

305
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,900
[ROBERT]
I'll keep my eyes peeled

306
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,567
next time we go out.

307
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,467
[PIA]  Team Alpha,

308
00:13:34,467 --> 00:13:37,467
<i>even if the Zafras
can't eliminate you</i>

309
00:13:37,467 --> 00:13:40,100
<i>like they did with
the other groups,</i>

310
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:44,733
<i>you'll suffer a worse fate
because of what I'm doing.</i>

311
00:13:46,067 --> 00:13:47,800
[KAREN] Sir Seb.

312
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,767
Yes?

313
00:13:48,767 --> 00:13:50,567
What's with the big smile?

314
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:51,567
Why?

315
00:13:51,567 --> 00:13:52,733
Is there a problem?

316
00:13:52,733 --> 00:13:56,800
Since you're the lead
in the search for Sam,

317
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:59,733
can I share some of
my observations?

318
00:13:59,733 --> 00:14:01,233
Go ahead. Let it rip.

319
00:14:01,233 --> 00:14:02,933
The team is out of focus.

320
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:05,100
It was evident
after what happened last night.

321
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:06,967
I don't know if
they're losing hope

322
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:10,000
or if we need to change
our strategy for this search.

323
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,567
Karen, are you losing hope?

324
00:14:13,567 --> 00:14:14,733
Of course not!

325
00:14:14,733 --> 00:14:16,667
Hope is the only thing
I'm holding onto now.

326
00:14:16,667 --> 00:14:18,967
Great. You and I both.

327
00:14:18,967 --> 00:14:21,000
We're both positive thinkers.

328
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,167
Now, Karen,
what we need to do

329
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:26,133
is share that optimism
with Team Alpha.

330
00:14:26,133 --> 00:14:28,133
We will find Sam.

331
00:14:28,167 --> 00:14:29,200
Trust me.

332
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:33,667
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:14:33,667 --> 00:14:37,000
[RALLOS] Are you saying I'm
useless to the investigation

334
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,267
because I'm only handling
paperwork, Borromeo?!

335
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:41,933
Cut it out, you two!

336
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:42,933
Enough!

337
00:14:42,933 --> 00:14:46,633
He agrees with
the NLEA's findings.

338
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:48,867
If they want to
investigate at First Creek,

339
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:49,867
then let them!

340
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:51,867
What if that could help us?

341
00:14:51,867 --> 00:14:53,533
They have their
own investigation

342
00:14:53,533 --> 00:14:55,000
and we have ours.

343
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Let's focus on
our own investigation!

344
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
[SEBASTIAN] Hey.
What's going on here?

345
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,300
Why are you fighting?

346
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,667
[BORROMEO] This guy thinks
he knows it all

347
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,200
and is siding with the NLEA.

348
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:07,033
Who do you work for?
The NCIA, remember?

349
00:15:07,033 --> 00:15:09,667
- I've had it with you!
- [CLAMORING]

350
00:15:09,667 --> 00:15:11,067
What are you doing?!

351
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:13,300
Are you trying to distract us
from the actual investigation?

352
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:14,700
What are you doing?!

353
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:17,900
I'm trying to make progress!

354
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:20,300
We're getting nowhere
with our search for Ma'am Sam.

355
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:22,133
The longer we go
without finding her,

356
00:15:22,133 --> 00:15:24,000
the more
we put her life in danger.

357
00:15:25,733 --> 00:15:27,733
[BORROMEO] Here's what we'll do.

358
00:15:27,733 --> 00:15:29,967
Since you want to find
Sam as soon as possible,

359
00:15:29,967 --> 00:15:31,900
come with us.

360
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:33,700
- Be useful out there.
- What did you say?!

361
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,300
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]
- Enough! Stop it!

362
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:37,033
What is going on?!

363
00:15:37,033 --> 00:15:41,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:15:41,333 --> 00:15:42,733
Nothing, sir.

365
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:45,067
We're just planning
our search for Ma'am Sam.

366
00:15:45,067 --> 00:15:48,067
Are you planning or fighting?

367
00:15:48,067 --> 00:15:49,267
Don't forget,

368
00:15:49,267 --> 00:15:53,400
you're working for
a government agency.

369
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:55,700
This isn't some fight club!

370
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:58,933
Things just got heated,
but don't worry.

371
00:15:58,933 --> 00:16:00,933
I'll talk to them.
I got this, sir.

372
00:16:00,933 --> 00:16:07,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

373
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:12,067
[SEBASTIAN'S MOUTH CLICKS,
SIGHS]

374
00:16:14,267 --> 00:16:15,867
[SHOUTING]

375
00:16:15,867 --> 00:16:16,867
Gabo!

376
00:16:16,867 --> 00:16:18,900
- Come on!
- Wait a minute!

377
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,767
- Please wait.
- Bring 'em over here.

378
00:16:20,767 --> 00:16:22,867
- Gabo!
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

379
00:16:22,867 --> 00:16:25,800
- Outsiders!
- Who are they?

380
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:28,167
We caught these outsiders
snooping around.

381
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:33,733
Maybe they're with
the group we fought last night!

382
00:16:33,733 --> 00:16:35,267
- Finish them off!
- [SHOUTING]

383
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:37,767
[CLAMORING, SHOUTING]

384
00:16:37,767 --> 00:16:38,933
Wait a minute!

385
00:16:38,933 --> 00:16:40,267
Stop! Stop!

386
00:16:42,233 --> 00:16:43,433
What brings you here?

387
00:16:43,433 --> 00:16:45,967
- [STAMMERING] I...
- What?!

388
00:16:45,967 --> 00:16:48,667
- [LAWIN] We're scavengers!
- [UWAK] We're scavengers!

389
00:16:48,667 --> 00:16:50,900
- Looking for food!
- We're scavenging!

390
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,200
[TOLITS] They're lying.

391
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:56,133
Maybe they really
are scavengers.

392
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:58,067
Where are you guys from?

393
00:16:58,067 --> 00:16:59,967
- From...
- Divisoria.

394
00:16:59,967 --> 00:17:02,067
[STAMMERING] Divisoria.

395
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:03,400
[BONG]
Are you telling the truth?

396
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,133
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

397
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:07,800
- We're telling the truth!
- Ow!

398
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:10,100
Gabo, I think these guys
are playing us.

399
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,133
Let's cut them up.

400
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:14,300
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

401
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,400
Wait!

402
00:17:15,433 --> 00:17:16,833
[LAWIN WHIMPERING]

403
00:17:16,833 --> 00:17:21,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

404
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:23,967
- You guys want to eat?
- Y-yes.

405
00:17:24,767 --> 00:17:26,033
Alright.

406
00:17:26,033 --> 00:17:27,833
- [TEKLA] But, Gabo...
- We'll feed you.

407
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:29,000
Don't fall for their act!

408
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
You got beaten up last night!
You almost died!

409
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,367
They might try
to trick you again!

410
00:17:32,367 --> 00:17:34,000
She's right, Gabo!

411
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,333
I feel bad for them.

412
00:17:35,333 --> 00:17:37,200
They look innocent.

413
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,000
And they're starving.

414
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,300
We have to help them.

415
00:17:42,167 --> 00:17:43,833
Come on. Eat at our place.

416
00:17:43,833 --> 00:17:45,800
- Thank you.
- You're going to believe them?

417
00:17:45,867 --> 00:17:47,133
Go on.

418
00:17:47,133 --> 00:17:48,767
Don't try anything stupid,
got it?

419
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,967
- Try us!
- We won't!

420
00:17:50,967 --> 00:17:52,333
- Watch yourself!
- Yes.

421
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:53,867
[MAMENG] Don't hurt them.

422
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:55,100
Yeah, don't hurt us.

423
00:17:56,733 --> 00:18:03,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

424
00:18:10,467 --> 00:18:12,467
[DISTANT GUNFIRE]

425
00:18:18,133 --> 00:18:21,333
Boss, I don't think
we're getting out of here alive.

426
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:24,233
Maybe they brought us here
to take us out.

427
00:18:24,233 --> 00:18:25,867
Shut up!

428
00:18:25,867 --> 00:18:28,400
If they wanted to shoot us,
they would've done it already.

429
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:31,067
We wouldn't have even
made it here.

430
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,367
I think...

431
00:18:35,367 --> 00:18:37,533
they're giving me
another chance.

432
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,367
They've got another job for me.

433
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:43,367
Even after we screwed up?

434
00:18:44,033 --> 00:18:46,033
That was the last time
I'll ever screw up!

435
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:51,933
As long as we're
with the Zafras,

436
00:18:51,933 --> 00:18:54,000
anyone who crosses me
is going down.

437
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,833
And that Gabo...

438
00:18:58,433 --> 00:19:00,533
...I'll grind him into the dirt.

439
00:19:02,067 --> 00:19:03,267
[SINISTER CHUCKLE]

440
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:05,533
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

441
00:19:07,367 --> 00:19:08,067
- Cheers!
- Whoo!

442
00:19:08,067 --> 00:19:09,633
Bottoms up!

443
00:19:09,633 --> 00:19:10,867
Let me try this.

444
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,467
[DJANGO SIGHS]

445
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:13,700
- [GLASS THUDS]
- [CLEARS THROAT]

446
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:14,933
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

447
00:19:14,933 --> 00:19:16,033
Let's finish every drop.

448
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:19,233
[INDISTINCT OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

449
00:19:19,233 --> 00:19:21,100
Grab that bottle and open it.

450
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:23,900
- [WIND WHOOSHING]
- [LEAVES RUSTLING]

451
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,867
- That's the one.
- This here?

452
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:30,033
Looks banging.

453
00:19:31,267 --> 00:19:33,033
Real smooth.

454
00:19:34,467 --> 00:19:35,933
Let's give you a bath.

455
00:19:35,933 --> 00:19:37,933
[LAUGHING]

456
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:40,467
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

457
00:19:40,467 --> 00:19:41,433
[GLASS THUDS]

458
00:19:42,933 --> 00:19:43,900
[SIGHS]

459
00:19:45,933 --> 00:19:47,267
[URINE TRICKLING]

460
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,467
Go meet them.

461
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,100
[GUN COCKS]

462
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:57,167
That's worth more
than your entire existence.

463
00:19:57,167 --> 00:19:58,167
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:19:58,167 --> 00:19:59,433
What are you doing here?

465
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,933
Wait, let me finish this--

466
00:20:01,233 --> 00:20:03,133
- [GOON 1] Move!
- [GOON 2] Drop down!

467
00:20:04,133 --> 00:20:05,233
[LAO] On your knees!

468
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,467
Weren't you the ones
who got in our way?

469
00:20:09,467 --> 00:20:11,267
You were all acting
cocky before.

470
00:20:11,267 --> 00:20:12,967
Where's that cockiness now?

471
00:20:12,967 --> 00:20:14,100
Wait a minute, a minute!

472
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,500
We were invited to come here!

473
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:16,667
Who are you kidding?

474
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:19,467
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

475
00:20:19,533 --> 00:20:22,300
[ARTURO]
Sir, your guests have arrived.

476
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:24,333
- [SNICKERS]
- [GLASS THUDS]

477
00:20:29,267 --> 00:20:30,267
[MARIANO] Lucas!

478
00:20:33,667 --> 00:20:35,167
They are not enemies.

479
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:38,400
Pa, we clashed with these guys.

480
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,533
What are they doing here?

481
00:20:40,533 --> 00:20:42,133
I asked them to come here.

482
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:45,633
They have unfinished business.

483
00:20:45,633 --> 00:20:48,000
[DEBORAH] We need
to get back the gold

484
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,300
that NLEA took from us.

485
00:20:51,133 --> 00:20:54,333
And you, Lucas...

486
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:57,800
...will be the leader
of this operation.

487
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:58,967
Wait a minute.

488
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:01,133
That wasn't part of the deal.

489
00:21:01,133 --> 00:21:03,033
I am the King of Tondo.

490
00:21:03,033 --> 00:21:04,367
[MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

491
00:21:04,467 --> 00:21:06,167
Nobody tells me what to do.

492
00:21:06,167 --> 00:21:07,133
[MARIANO SCOFFS]

493
00:21:10,267 --> 00:21:11,833
You're not in Tondo.

494
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:15,100
And this isn't some small
side hustle we're making you do.

495
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:19,033
We've given you the chance
to enter our world,

496
00:21:19,033 --> 00:21:21,067
so you'd better learn
to play by the rules.

497
00:21:21,067 --> 00:21:28,033
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:32,300
Yes, ma'am.

499
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:35,633
Put down your guns!

500
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,733
Follow me.

501
00:21:41,867 --> 00:21:43,300
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

502
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:49,767
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

503
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:54,733
Sir?

504
00:21:54,733 --> 00:21:57,167
I heard things got intense
back there.

505
00:21:57,533 --> 00:21:58,700
Is that true?

506
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,067
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

507
00:22:00,067 --> 00:22:02,333
We've been looking for Sam
for days.

508
00:22:02,767 --> 00:22:04,500
I understand them.

509
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:09,200
They're panicking
and feeling disappointed.

510
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:11,167
But how can we find her

511
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:14,100
when we're in such a mess?

512
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:16,100
[PIA EXHALES HEAVILY]

513
00:22:16,133 --> 00:22:20,800
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

514
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,667
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

515
00:22:22,667 --> 00:22:24,067
Um...
[CLICKS TONGUE]

516
00:22:26,433 --> 00:22:28,400
I guess it's good that...

517
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:32,100
we can express
what we truly feel,

518
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:35,233
even if it might hurt
our colleagues.

519
00:22:35,233 --> 00:22:37,600
At least it lightens the...

520
00:22:38,167 --> 00:22:40,233
the burden we're carrying.

521
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:42,133
It's been rough.

522
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:49,100
The case has become
too personal for my agents.

523
00:22:49,133 --> 00:22:50,633
Exactly.

524
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:55,200
Team Alpha is taking Jacinto's
disappearance too personally.

525
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,433
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

526
00:22:56,433 --> 00:22:58,133
And so are you, sir.

527
00:22:58,133 --> 00:23:00,767
This matter has become
too personal for you.

528
00:23:00,767 --> 00:23:01,800
Hasn't it?

529
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,200
[MUSIC ENDS]

530
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:06,267
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

531
00:23:06,267 --> 00:23:07,733
[SCREEN DOOR SQUEAKING]

532
00:23:09,133 --> 00:23:10,167
[GABO] Have a seat.

533
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:13,700
[CHAIR RATTLES]

534
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:14,733
I'm sorry.

535
00:23:16,767 --> 00:23:17,733
[GROANS WEAKLY]

536
00:23:18,833 --> 00:23:19,867
Love...

537
00:23:19,867 --> 00:23:22,767
Can you help me
give them some food?

538
00:23:23,833 --> 00:23:25,533
Is it okay if I use these?

539
00:23:25,533 --> 00:23:28,300
It's fine. I'll just explain it
to Auntie Betchay later.

540
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:29,400
I'll buy some next time.

541
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,467
Okay.

542
00:23:30,467 --> 00:23:31,967
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

543
00:23:31,967 --> 00:23:34,200
[PLATES RATTLING]

544
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:35,833
[LAWIN STAMMERING]

545
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:37,133
T-Thanks...

546
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:38,600
I'm sorry.

547
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:40,500
About...

548
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:43,333
...what my friends did
to you both.

549
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,433
[LAWIN] It's... okay.

550
00:23:47,333 --> 00:23:49,467
Here you go,
some dipping sauce.

551
00:23:49,467 --> 00:23:51,767
[LAWIN CLAPPING, STAMMERING]

552
00:23:53,533 --> 00:23:56,600
Love, can you please grab
the medicine kit?

553
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:01,167
We'll clean up
their cuts and scrapes.

554
00:24:01,567 --> 00:24:02,933
Sure, I've got it.

555
00:24:02,933 --> 00:24:05,167
If you need anything,
just shout. I'll grab the meds.

556
00:24:05,233 --> 00:24:06,533
[LAWIN] T-Thank you.

557
00:24:07,767 --> 00:24:10,233
[LAWIN SLAMS TABLE, MUMBLES]

558
00:24:10,233 --> 00:24:11,833
- [GROANS]
- [COUGHS]

559
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:13,700
Those bastards...

560
00:24:13,700 --> 00:24:16,200
Your friends outside
gave us a serious beating.

561
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,767
Not too loud.

562
00:24:17,767 --> 00:24:19,300
Someone might hear you.

563
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,500
[TEKLA]
My goodness, Uncle Rudy!

564
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:26,467
Your son is way too trusting!

565
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:28,967
[MAMENG] Where did you
even find those two?

566
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:32,400
[TOLITS] They were walking
down the alley, Auntie Mameng.

567
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,367
We checked their faces,
but couldn't recognize them.

568
00:24:34,367 --> 00:24:37,567
Maybe they're enemies
in disguise.

569
00:24:37,567 --> 00:24:39,367
Why didn't you take them out?

570
00:24:39,367 --> 00:24:40,967
- You even brought them here.
- [MAMENG] Hey now...

571
00:24:40,967 --> 00:24:43,567
[DABOY] We weren't sure,
so we figured Gabo should know.

572
00:24:43,567 --> 00:24:45,800
Could it be that
you've made a mistake?

573
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:49,033
Maybe they just happen
to be here to scavenge.

574
00:24:49,033 --> 00:24:49,967
Yeah.

575
00:24:49,967 --> 00:24:52,300
You can't blame us, Uncle Rudy.

576
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:53,700
It's hard to trust nowadays.

577
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:55,400
We need to be extra cautious.

578
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:56,733
Gabo told us that.

579
00:24:56,733 --> 00:24:59,533
You know what, Rudy,
your son is very kind.

580
00:24:59,533 --> 00:25:02,667
He can get too much sometimes,
but he has a big heart.

581
00:25:08,567 --> 00:25:10,233
[SAM]  Gabo is really kind.

582
00:25:11,300 --> 00:25:12,767
<i> I can't believe it.</i>

583
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:18,400
Why are you here anyway?

584
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:20,000
Pops sent us here.

585
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,733
Why?

586
00:25:21,733 --> 00:25:24,567
- Do I have a mission?
- Yes.

587
00:25:24,567 --> 00:25:28,467
Tomorrow we'll send the details
of your mission to your tablet.

588
00:25:28,467 --> 00:25:29,967
Gabo, don't let us down.

589
00:25:29,967 --> 00:25:32,967
Prove to Pops you're worthy
of this role, alright?

590
00:25:32,967 --> 00:25:36,633
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

591
00:25:36,667 --> 00:25:37,833
Don't worry.

592
00:25:37,833 --> 00:25:39,967
I'll do everything
to succeed in my mission.

593
00:25:43,533 --> 00:25:44,967
<i> In all fairness to him...</i>

594
00:25:44,967 --> 00:25:46,600
[MUSIC TURNS SOFT]

595
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:48,333
<i> from what I've seen,</i>

596
00:25:48,333 --> 00:25:50,000
<i> the more I get to know him,</i>

597
00:25:51,033 --> 00:25:52,900
<i>the more I realize
he has a heart of gold.</i>

598
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,567
<i> He really is helpful.</i>

599
00:25:56,633 --> 00:25:59,967
<i>He even saved the parents
of those children.</i>

600
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,300
<i>And now he's feeding
those strangers.</i>

601
00:26:06,433 --> 00:26:08,000
<i>I'm slowly
getting to know him better.</i>

602
00:26:09,667 --> 00:26:13,833
<i>I just hope everything
he has shown me is real.</i>

603
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:23,067
Wait.

604
00:26:23,067 --> 00:26:24,200
Who's that woman?

605
00:26:25,233 --> 00:26:26,767
Oh... That's my wife.

606
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:30,133
Gloria.

607
00:26:30,133 --> 00:26:31,200
[CHUCKLES]

608
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,867
You've got good taste, boy.

609
00:26:34,033 --> 00:26:35,167
She's beautiful.

610
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:37,933
Where did you meet her?

611
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:40,500
That's none of your business.

612
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:42,300
- [GLORIA] Gabo?
- [STAMMERING] I...

613
00:26:42,333 --> 00:26:44,900
- Gabo?
- Thank you.

614
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:48,000
- T-thank you...
- Here's your medicine.

615
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,867
- W-we should go.
- Yes.

616
00:26:49,867 --> 00:26:51,833
Oh, wait.
You haven't finished eating.

617
00:26:51,833 --> 00:26:54,000
- Thank you.
- We're leaving now.

618
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,667
We might finish all your food.

619
00:26:55,667 --> 00:26:58,167
- Let me look at your wounds!
- [LAWIN] Thank you.

620
00:26:58,167 --> 00:26:59,900
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

621
00:26:59,900 --> 00:27:02,333
Gabo, why did they leave?
Do they not want the food?

622
00:27:02,333 --> 00:27:04,633
I do not know why they left
so suddenly.

623
00:27:05,067 --> 00:27:07,067
We haven't even treated
their wounds yet.

624
00:27:07,067 --> 00:27:09,067
- There they are!
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

625
00:27:09,067 --> 00:27:11,733
- Let's go!
- Where are you going?

626
00:27:11,733 --> 00:27:13,200
We're leaving.
Thank you so much.

627
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:15,200
Thank you for the food
and for letting us stay.

628
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:17,933
- We'll walk you out.
- No, it is okay. Thanks.

629
00:27:17,967 --> 00:27:19,867
[TOLITS]
You might get in trouble!

630
00:27:19,867 --> 00:27:21,800
- We can handle it.
- They speak well?

631
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:22,900
- Right?
- See?

632
00:27:22,900 --> 00:27:24,733
They were stuttering
when they came in,

633
00:27:24,733 --> 00:27:26,767
but their speech was
perfectly fine when they left.

634
00:27:26,767 --> 00:27:28,900
- They were just pretending!
- I knew it.

635
00:27:28,900 --> 00:27:30,033
Honey.

636
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:37,167
I might leave first thing
tomorrow morning.

637
00:27:38,300 --> 00:27:41,133
I am just going to look for...

638
00:27:41,133 --> 00:27:42,667
for a job.

639
00:27:44,033 --> 00:27:45,300
I have been thinking...

640
00:27:45,300 --> 00:27:50,200
maybe I need to find a
steady job for the two of us.

641
00:27:50,233 --> 00:27:52,900
For the family
we're going to have.

642
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:56,267
That sounds wonderful.

643
00:27:56,900 --> 00:27:58,033
But...

644
00:27:58,733 --> 00:28:01,033
did you finish school?

645
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,200
No.

646
00:28:04,233 --> 00:28:06,733
I didn't even
make it to college.

647
00:28:06,733 --> 00:28:08,600
But that's okay.

648
00:28:08,600 --> 00:28:11,233
I'm sure I'll find
plenty of jobs out there.

649
00:28:11,233 --> 00:28:13,133
I know how to do
a lot of things.

650
00:28:13,133 --> 00:28:14,233
Don't worry.

651
00:28:14,233 --> 00:28:16,200
I'm sure I'll find
a job tomorrow.

652
00:28:17,133 --> 00:28:20,933
That'll help improve
our situation here a little.

653
00:28:23,700 --> 00:28:25,033
Wait.

654
00:28:25,033 --> 00:28:26,267
It's a legal job, right?

655
00:28:26,267 --> 00:28:29,267
Yeah. I wouldn't...

656
00:28:29,267 --> 00:28:32,633
take any illegal job, Love.

657
00:28:36,867 --> 00:28:40,367
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

658
00:28:40,367 --> 00:28:43,100
Of course, Love.
I've been thinking...

659
00:28:45,167 --> 00:28:48,933
I need to get a proper job
so you can be proud of me.

660
00:28:49,767 --> 00:28:52,233
So we can prepare for the
family we're building.

661
00:28:52,967 --> 00:28:56,233
Because when we have kids...

662
00:28:57,700 --> 00:28:59,667
I want them to be proud of me.

663
00:29:01,867 --> 00:29:03,300
I'm sorry, Love.

664
00:29:03,300 --> 00:29:05,167
Life has been pretty
hard for us.

665
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:10,033
But I promise you,
I will make things right.

666
00:29:11,133 --> 00:29:13,033
When we have a family,

667
00:29:13,033 --> 00:29:15,200
I want to give you all
a good life.

668
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:17,633
I will give you everything
you need.

669
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:25,767
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

670
00:29:26,833 --> 00:29:28,267
[SAM]  What's going on?

671
00:29:30,333 --> 00:29:33,067
<i>How is he such
a perfect husband?</i>

672
00:29:35,167 --> 00:29:36,933
<i> Do people like him even exist?</i>

673
00:29:36,933 --> 00:29:43,800
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

674
00:29:46,100 --> 00:29:48,100
<i>So, how did I end up
falling for you?</i>

675
00:29:48,100 --> 00:29:50,500
<i>Of course, you fell for me
because I'm handsome.</i>

676
00:29:50,500 --> 00:29:52,600
<i> He's not pretending anymore.</i>

677
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:57,000
<i>I really think he is falling
for Gloria.</i>

678
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,733
<i>We found Sam's jacket
in the river.</i>

679
00:29:59,733 --> 00:30:02,100
<i>- It was riddled with bullets.
- Where did you find this?</i>

680
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:03,400
<i> In Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

681
00:30:03,433 --> 00:30:05,200
<i> Once Uncle Rudy signs it,</i>

682
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,567
<i>he is agreeing to have
all of you</i>

683
00:30:06,567 --> 00:30:09,367
<i>evicted from Ginintuang Lupa
in exchange for money.</i>

684
00:30:09,367 --> 00:30:11,233
<i>General Jacinto
is pushing through</i>

685
00:30:11,233 --> 00:30:12,733
<i>with the demolition
of Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

686
00:30:12,733 --> 00:30:15,533
<i>We're after a criminal.
He entered Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

687
00:30:15,533 --> 00:30:17,467
<i>Let's see
if he can escape this one,</i>

688
00:30:17,467 --> 00:30:19,467
<i>now that NLEA itself
are the ones chasing him down.</i>

689
00:30:19,467 --> 00:30:23,467
<i>Isn't the long-haired man
Sam's person of interest?</i>

690
00:30:23,467 --> 00:30:24,633
<i> This guy...</i>

691
00:30:24,633 --> 00:30:26,633
<i>He knows a lot
about the Zafras.</i>

692
00:30:26,633 --> 00:30:28,200
<i> We need to find him.</i>

693
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:31,400
<i>He's the key to bringing
the Zafras to justice.</i>

694
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:33,800
<i>I never thought you would
come into my life.</i>

695
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,633
I hope this is not just a dream.

696
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:37,833
Whatever I'm feeling right now,

697
00:30:37,833 --> 00:30:39,500
<i> I hope it will last forever.</i>

698
00:30:39,500 --> 00:30:41,267
<i>I just want you to know,
Gloria...</i>

699
00:30:41,267 --> 00:30:42,533
<i> I love you so much.</i>
